        "original_id": "2f235db4-890f-54c8-8e4a-1a00470cf0fe",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Phoenix, Arizona; Piestewa Peak Recreation Area; Phoenix Mountain Preserve\n- Systems: Arizona State Route 51; Piestewa Freeway; Piestewa Parkway\n- People: Lori Piestewa\n- Organizations: U.S. military; Hopi tribe\n\nFacts:\n- Arizona State Route 51 is a numbered state highway in Phoenix, Arizona, and it is also known as the Piestewa Freeway.\n- Lori Piestewa was a member of the Hopi tribe.\n- Lori Piestewa was the first Native American woman in history to die in combat while serving in the U.S. military.\n- Lori Piestewa was the first woman in the U.S. military killed in the Iraq War.\n- Piestewa Peak was named after Lori Piestewa.\n- Piestewa Peak is located in the Piestewa Peak Recreation Area within the Phoenix Mountain Preserve, near Piestewa Parkway, which is Arizona State Route 51.",
